  longerTitle: Pets
  description: 'Having pets can increase the time needed to evacuate safely. It is
    very important to make plans in advance and consider multiple scenarios and consequences
    of choices. Be sure you have a carrier or leash readily available and that the
    pets are in an easily accessible space on red flag days (ie. keep them inside
    and in a room where you can find/catch them easily). It may be a good idea to
    evacuate early and have a plan to stay in a pet-friendly shelter or with friends.

'
